---
name: refine-pixel-art
description: Refine an accepted pixel-art identity, view, action study or selected set into reviewed native PNG masters. Use generated adaptation only when needed and deterministic normalization; separate technical checks from visual acceptance, without claiming hand-pixel cleanup.
---

# Refine Pixel Art

Read `references/runtime.md` before using tools or scripts. Refine a single accepted design or an explicitly selected set at any workflow point; animation is optional.

## Choose the scope

Read `references/project-contract.md`. Inspect requested assets, accepted identity/profile and approval evidence. Obtain missing design acceptance or route to the relevant design skill; ask only for blocking choices.
- **Standalone native asset or selected set:** Use the compact record/helper contract in `references/standalone-records.md`. Keep `project.json`/`profile.json` for pipeline helpers without requiring a full run directory or portable bundle.
- **Requested multi-stage workflow, cross-session continuation or portable handoff:** Read `references/run-records.md` and `references/portable-handoff.md`. Check supplied bundles, inspect their assets and continue their records, approval scope and remaining budget rather than resetting counters or relying on hidden history.

Lock native canvas, views, palette roles/limit, alpha, padding, anchor convention, downstream use and identity invariants. For sets, record common camera/projection where relevant, body scale, normalization geometry, approved palette mapping and legitimate per-view deviations. Required missing members remain blockers. Set bounded generation/repair allowances; count every failed/cancelled/pending start across stages and sessions.

## Adapt, normalize, accept

1. If the source already fits technically and visually, retain its exact PNG bytes and review it without regeneration or lossy conversion. Otherwise use imagegen for native-grid adaptation and creative repairs, preserving identity and pose. Inspect and use exact nearest-neighbor enlargements of accepted native references as primary pixel references; concepts are supplementary. Request deliberate clusters, readable face/hands/props and appropriate clearance. Never paint fixes or draw replacement art in code.
2. Before each call record exact prompt, actual arguments and reference roles/hashes. Preserve every returned original unchanged in a unique attempt path, retain rejections and measure real dimensions/cell geometry. Normalize via `prepare_pixels.sh --project project.json`; see `references/pixel-tooling.md`. Use measured matching-aspect geometry, nearest-neighbor sampling, no dither, approved palette and binary alpha. Do not trim/recenter set members, stretch wrong aspects or bypass an incompatible grid lock. Repair observed defects within caps; leave `needs_revision` at exhaustion.
3. Review each native PNG at 1× and integer enlargement for silhouette, clusters, gaze, anatomy, costume/material roles, prop contacts and padding. Measure bounds, margins and root/ground anchors. Technical normalization cannot establish identity, craft or action readability.
4. Compare selected set members together for size/grid, palette and material roles, proportions/apparent scale, anchors, accessory side and identity. View-dependent silhouette widths are legitimate. Revalidate the entire set after shared palette/grid changes; separate good-looking assets do not prove a consistent set.
5. For planned animation read `references/action-continuity.md` and check contacts, moving-material separation, trajectory clearance and stable root. For local motion read `references/local-motion.md` before generation or mask planning: review the **whole original moving part**, **swept envelope** and **vacated area**, including attachment/outline pixels and protected old-part remnants. Full-body motion uses identity/root/contact/scale criteria, not a stationary-pixel lock. A neutral master may still need action design for a particular action.
6. Run native QA in static/refinement scope, honoring format and set requirements without pretending to satisfy future animation timing/drawing counts. Keep separate technical and visual statuses, including failed or unverified checks.
7. Accept each native master and the set separately under user approval or quoted creative delegation. Record actual actor/scope, exact hash, dimensions, source/normalization provenance, palette/anchor and limitations. A helper exit code cannot grant approval; never call delegated acceptance user approval of unseen pixels. Preserve accepted PNGs byte-for-byte.

## Deliver

Provide selected native PNGs, preserved sources, integer previews and compact technical/visual/set/action-readiness, approval and remaining-budget records. Distinguish studies from `native_master` assets, retaining source-role/view/pose mapping. Only the full/continuation path adds a self-contained bundle and copied-bundle check.

For animation supply actual accepted native masters, exact hashes, normalization geometry, palette, anchor/contact/scale limits and approval scope. Their exact integer enlargement must remain the primary generation reference; an earlier large concept cannot replace it. A later creative master change requires renewed native acceptance here.

For difficult or uncertain stills, optional independent review follows `references/visual-review.md`; routine single-image work does not require an extra reviewer.
